"""providers — vault-owned API-key store for AI providers.

Canonical credentials live in vaultwarden (folder llm, items named
{PROVIDER}_API_KEY per the C1 convention). A local 0600 cache serves
offline/headless contexts. This tool also maintains the OpenCode and shell
credential mirrors plus live model catalogs for OpenCode, Hermes, and Pi-based
tools such as Miniharness.

Commands:
  (no args)                    Refresh model lists for all enabled providers
  <provider>                   Refresh model list for one enabled provider
  --list                       List configured provider names
  auth                         Interactive API key enrollment (prompts per provider)
  auth <provider> <key>        Write key directly (agent-friendly)
  ls                           List providers and enrollment status (never the key)
  timer enable                 Install the hourly systemd/launchd timer
  timer disable                Remove the hourly timer
  timer status                 Show timer state and next run
  sync                         vault -> cache -> opencode auth.json -> .zshenv
  capabilities show ... --json Read the last-known-good model capability cache
  capabilities refresh ... --json
                               Refresh model capabilities once, then print JSON
  audit                        List vault llm items, flag non-conforming names
  rename [--dry-run|--apply]   Enforce the C1 naming convention on vault items
  add                          Add a provider interactively
  add <provider> <url> <key> [model]
                               Add directly; model is required without /models
  enable <provider>            Enable a provider that has an API key
  disable <provider>           Disable a provider without deleting its key
"""

